    choose: [['I should have (respected / respect) that.', 'respected'], ['I shouldn\'t have (asked / asking) you to stay.', 'asked'], ['I take responsibility (for / at) my choice.', 'for'], ['I need to (figure / figured) things out.', 'figure'], ['Let\'s focus (on / to) the handover.', 'on'], ['Please use the project channel (for / since) work questions.', 'for']],
    choices: [['"I still have feelings, but I hear your decision." What does still mean?', 'The feelings continue.', 'The feelings never existed.', 'A'], ['"Use only the project channel for work." What is requested?', 'Arrange a private dinner.', 'Keep contact in the work channel.', 'B'], ['"I should have respected that." What is expressed?', 'Regret about a past action.', 'Confirmation that everything is repaired.', 'A'], ['Which detail is a work arrangement?', 'Emma has agreed to date Ren.', 'The handover is at ten.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: ['You are Emma. Your tutor reads Ren\'s follow-up message, then plays Nao during a short call. Explain what Ren agreed to do and what you have decided about work contact.', 'あなたはエマ役です。講師はレンの追加の連絡を読んでから、短い電話でナオ役になります。レンが同意したことと、自分が決めた仕事の連絡方法を説明しましょう。'], task: ['Listen for the channel, meeting arrangement, and contact Ren says he will avoid. Tell Nao the confirmed details and explain why these do not mean you have started a new relationship.', '連絡先、会議の予定、レンが控える連絡を聞き取りましょう。ナオに確定した情報を伝え、それが新しい交際を始めたという意味ではないことを説明しましょう。'], roles: ['Nao', 'Emma'], text: '<p>I have posted the handover notes in the team channel. Our project meeting is Friday at eleven in the office, with the team lead present. I will not send private invitations. If the client changes the brief, I will post it where the whole team can see it. I know this is about working professionally, not starting a relationship.</p>', lines: ['Emma, what has Ren agreed about work contact?', 'Where are the handover notes?', 'When is the next project meeting, and who will be there?', 'What will he do if the client changes the brief?', 'Does this message mean you two are starting a relationship?', 'What responsibility do you still need to take with Leo?'], evidence: 'Team channel for notes/changes, Friday eleven office with team lead, no private invitations, professional contact not a new relationship. Do not invent reconciliation with Leo. Assess listening evidence separately from grammar in the explanation.', useful: ['He has agreed to ...', 'The notes are in ...', 'The meeting is ...', 'He will not ...', 'That does not mean ...', 'I still need to ...'] },
