    trivia: ['"I hear you" can mean "I understand your point," not just that a sound reached you. It acknowledges what someone said, but the next sentence and actions show whether a request is accepted.', 'I hear you. は、単に音が聞こえるだけでなく「言いたいことは分かります」という意味にもなります。その後の言葉や行動で、要望を受け入れたかを確かめましょう。'], triviaQuestion: ['Can "I hear you" acknowledge someone\'s point without describing a sound problem?', 'Yes.'],
