    apply: { situation: ['Read Claire and Nao\'s notes after their discussion. Compare their reasons and the final agreement.', '話し合いの後のクレアとナオのメモを読みましょう。理由と最後の合意を比べましょう。'], text: '<p><strong>Claire\'s view</strong><br>Emma should explain properly and show that she is sorry. A clear apology could help because Leo needs the truth. I first thought we should arrange a meeting.</p><p><strong>Nao\'s view</strong><br>Although Emma has apologized, Leo is still hurt. He needs time. We should not arrange a meeting unless both agree.</p><p><strong>What we agreed</strong><br>Offer to listen to each friend. Ask before passing on a message. Do not invite them to a surprise meeting or promise that they will get back together.</p>', questions: [['Why does Claire value an apology?', 'Leo needs the truth and a clear explanation.'], ['Why does Nao oppose an arranged meeting without agreement?', 'Leo is still hurt and needs time.'], ['Did they agree to Claire\'s first meeting idea?', 'No. They agreed to ask first.'], ['What action do both support?', 'Listening, asking before passing messages, and not deciding for their friends.']] },
    choose: [['Although she (apologized / apologizing), he is still hurt.', 'apologized'], ['I see your (point / pointed).', 'point'], ['We should ask before (arranging / arrange) a meeting.', 'arranging'], ['Let\'s avoid (deciding / decide) for them.', 'deciding'], ['We can agree (on / to with) one thing.', 'on'], ['He needs time. (However / Because of that he), we can still offer support.', 'However']],
    choices: [['Claire first suggests a meeting. What is the final agreement?', 'Arrange a surprise meeting.', 'Ask both friends before arranging anything.', 'B'], ['Which sentence keeps both facts?', 'Although she apologized, he is still hurt.', 'Her apology proves he is no longer hurt.', 'A'], ['Which reply acknowledges a reason before disagreeing?', 'That idea is stupid.', 'I see your point, but he has asked for time.', 'B'], ['What does supporting a friend mean in their final plan?', 'Listen and respect the friend\'s decision.', 'Choose the relationship outcome for them.', 'A']],
    mission: { situation: ['You are Claire. Your tutor is Nao. Read a new proposal for Friday\'s cafe gathering and Leo\'s reply. Decide how to change the plan without pressuring either friend.', 'あなたはクレア役、講師はナオ役です。金曜日のカフェの集まりへの新しい提案とレオの返事を読みましょう。どちらの友達にも無理をさせず、案をどう変えるか考えましょう。'], task: ['Compare the proposal with Leo\'s stated request. Explain one concern, disagree politely with an unsuitable idea, and agree on a revised action based on the messages.', '提案とレオの希望を比べましょう。心配を一つ説明し、合わない案には丁寧に反対して、メッセージを根拠に変更案を決めましょう。'], roles: ['Nao', 'Claire'], title: 'Friday Gathering - A Proposal and a Reply', text: '<p><strong>Initial proposal</strong><br>Invite Emma and Leo to the same table on Friday at seven. Perhaps a relaxed meal would help them talk.</p><p><strong>Leo\'s reply</strong><br>Thanks for thinking of me. I do not want a group meal with Emma this week. Please do not surprise me with one. I can help prepare the cafe before six, then I want to leave.</p><p><strong>Emma\'s message</strong><br>I am not attending the meal. Please ask me before sharing my private messages.</p><p><strong>Decision needed</strong><br>Keep the ordinary gathering separate from the relationship discussion. Confirm Leo\'s preparation time and ask before passing on any personal message.</p>', lines: ['Claire, do you still think we should invite them to the same table?', 'What does Leo actually agree to do on Friday?', 'Although the meal might feel relaxed to us, what concern do you see?', 'What should we do with Emma\'s private messages?', 'What revised plan can we both support?'], evidence: 'No shared-table surprise; Leo prepares before six then leaves, not attending seven meal; Emma absent and wants permission for messages; keep gathering separate and respect requests. Cite the new card, not memory of Apply. Tutor does not insist on arranging reconciliation.', useful: ['The message says ...', 'Although ..., ...', 'I see your point, but ...', 'He has only agreed to ...', 'We should ask before ...', 'Can we agree to ...?'] },
    topics: [['DIFFERENT VIEWS', ['How do you explain the reason for an opinion?', 'What phrase helps you disagree politely?', 'How do you find common ground?']], ['PLANNING WITH OTHERS', ['What should you ask before making plans for someone?', 'How do you clarify a limited agreement?', 'What would you do if someone declined?']], ['PASSING ON MESSAGES', ['When should you ask before sharing a message?', 'How do you check the exact wording?', 'What can you say if you do not have permission?']]],
    trivia: ['"Agree with someone" usually refers to sharing an opinion. "Agree to do something" means accepting an action. "Agree on a time" means reaching a shared decision about that detail.', 'agree with someone は相手の意見への賛成、agree to do something は行動への同意、agree on a time は時刻について意見が一致することを表します。'], triviaQuestion: ['Which phrase confirms an action: agree to help or agree with an opinion?', 'Agree to help.'],
